diff --git a/FAQ.md b/FAQ.md
index 0642229..82fdcab 100644
--- a/FAQ.md
+++ b/FAQ.md
@@ -225,9 +225,13 @@ Advancement is not gated by any point system in the VTT — it's applied wheneve
 
 The illumination track is a 0–12 numeric value on the Circle. Players can increment it (the GM can also edit it directly). Every time it hits a multiple of 3 (3, 6, 9), the server fires a campaign-wide milestone notification. At 12, the track rolls over: `new_value = current - 12`, representing the circle completing a full chapter of illumination.
 
+### How do the circle's resources come back?
+
+On their own, by the book (p. 41). A new circle starts with 1 plus its members in each of Stitch, Refresh and Train (since 2026-10-13 also when its desk was first opened after members were approved: it used to start at 1 each until the seal). Spent resources do not come back after an assignment: when the circle advances on a full Illumination track, each refills to 1 plus the members. There is no Refill button (Robert's issue #66.4, 2026-10-13). A circle with Resource Management earns one back at each milestone (3, 6 and 9): the milestone's log line says so, the Lightkeeper's circle page (and on a wide desk the charter abstract) asks "Resource Management: earn back one" with Stitch, Refresh and Train, and one press applies the circle's choice and logs it ("Resource Management: The Moths earns back a Stitch (2 of 4)."). A full resource cannot be picked; with every resource full when the milestone passes there is nothing to earn back, and the log says that instead. Several milestones passed at once wait as several. Taking the track back past a milestone (a point added by mistake) takes its earn-back away, and the advance's refill clears any still waiting. The players' circle page says when one waits. The Lightkeeper's squares on each resource stay for corrections, and each press writes a log line ("The Lightkeeper set the circle's Train to 3 (was 2).").
+
 ### What is an assignment's report worth?
 
-By the book (p. 55): 1 Illumination for each of the circle's three Illumination questions answered yes, then for the Illumination Keys 2 if some of the investigators fulfilled one and 4 if every one of them did (nothing if none did). Since 2026-10-10 the Lightkeeper ticks the three questions once, for the circle, on their Circle page, and the players' reports carry only their keys. Under the report cards the page totals it (a living investigator with no report filed counts as no key) and adds it with one press, "Add N Illumination", once per assignment. The ticks and the added total are kept on the circle, so every Lightkeeper desk (another tab, another device) shows them and "Added N Illumination" once it is pressed; the server refuses a second add. End Assignment clears the reports and the tally, and its confirm warns when the reports' Illumination is not added yet, since it would be lost. Since 2026-10-12 (playtest 3, missing-report-silent) both name the living investigators who have not filed a report, "Not filed: Ada Quill.", once reports are due (the Lightkeeper has opened them, or someone has filed): over the Add N Illumination button until the tally is added, and in End Assignment's confirm. Before reports are due neither names anyone. Neither waits for them, and a report not filed still counts as no key. Every change to the track is logged, such as "The Ninth Night gains 2 Illumination (3 to 5)." Before, each player's report carried the three questions too, so one yes could come in four times, nothing totalled the reports, and the playtest's circle counted keys at 1 each and advanced about 5 Illumination early.
+By the book (p. 55): 1 Illumination for each of the circle's three Illumination questions answered yes, then for the Illumination Keys 2 if some of the investigators fulfilled one and 4 if every one of them did (nothing if none did). Since 2026-10-10 the Lightkeeper ticks the three questions once, for the circle, on their Circle page, and the players' reports carry only their keys. Since 2026-10-13 (Robert's issue #66.5) the page says what the questions are for, "Answered together at the end of an assignment: each yes adds 1 Illumination.", and the keys line reads "Investigators who fulfilled a key: 1 of 3" with what it adds beside it (+2); what a key is and the 2-or-4 rule are behind its "i". Under the report cards the page totals it (a living investigator with no report filed counts as no key) and adds it with one press, "Add N Illumination", once per assignment. The ticks and the added total are kept on the circle, so every Lightkeeper desk (another tab, another device) shows them and "Added N Illumination" once it is pressed; the server refuses a second add. End Assignment clears the reports and the tally, and its confirm warns when the reports' Illumination is not added yet, since it would be lost. Since 2026-10-12 (playtest 3, missing-report-silent) both name the living investigators who have not filed a report, "Not filed: Ada Quill.", once reports are due (the Lightkeeper has opened them, or someone has filed): over the Add N Illumination button until the tally is added, and in End Assignment's confirm. Before reports are due neither names anyone. Neither waits for them, and a report not filed still counts as no key. Every change to the track is logged, such as "The Ninth Night gains 2 Illumination (3 to 5)." Before, each player's report carried the three questions too, so one yes could come in four times, nothing totalled the reports, and the playtest's circle counted keys at 1 each and advanced about 5 Illumination early.
 
